/001-planner-turn-001.md:27:Split tool-result rendering into deterministic full-band truncation and smooth-band summaries with tiers and per-tool guidance.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:34:**Objective:** render tool results at the right fidelity per band while retaining full source results and removing `tool_call_summary`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:38:- Smooth-band `tool_result_summary` produced off the hot path for in-threshold results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:41:- Removal of `tool_call_summary`; tool-call arguments render as-is.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:52:**AC-2.1:** Full-band tool-result shortening uses deterministic truncation with no model call (the Epic 03 visibility-boundary floor).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:55:  - Given: a large tool result aged past the visibility boundary\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:59:**AC-2.2:** Smooth-band tool-result rendering uses an inference `tool_result_summary`, produced off the hot path.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:62:  - Given: a tool result in a turn assigned to the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:69:  - Given: a tool result under ~1000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:73:  - Given: a tool result between ~1000 and ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:77:  - Given: a tool result beyond ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:84:  - Given: tool results from two different tools\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:88:  - Given: a failed tool result\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:92:**AC-2.5:** The `tool_call_summary` derivation type is removed; tool-call arguments render as-is wherever a tool call appears.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:94:- **TC-2.5a:** No tool_call_summary derivation\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:97:  - Then: no `tool_call_summary` derivation exists or is queued\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:103:**AC-2.6:** The full tool result is always retained in the record regardless of how it is rendered in any band.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:106:  - Given: a tool result that is truncated in the full band and summarized in the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:108:  - Then: the original full tool result is intact\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:110:**AC-2.7:** A tool result beyond the large-tier threshold satisfies its `tool_result_summary` by deterministic truncation and lands `ready` without inference (no inference work item is created for it).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:113:  - Given: a tool result beyond ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:115:  - Then: the `tool_result_summary` is the deterministic truncation, state is `ready`, and no inference work item was created\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:117:**AC-2.8:** When the background worker's in-threshold tool-result inference terminally fails, the derivation lands `failed` with its reason — the worker records the honest failure rather than flooring it. Consumers recover to the truncation floor and resolve it to `ready` at construction (Flow 3).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:120:  - Given: tool-result inference exhausts its retry budget for an in-threshold result\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:129:Story 2 separates tool-result rendering by band. Full-band shortening uses the existing deterministic truncation floor. Smooth-band rendering uses `tool_result_summary` for in-threshold results and deterministic truncation for large results, which lands `ready` without creating inference work.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:131:Tool calls are not summarized. Removing `tool_call_summary` must reach the derivation kind set, work-queue registry, compose part plans, provider interface, deterministic provider, and prompt surface. Full source tool results remain canonical and intact.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:138:- Tier gates and removal of `tool_call_summary` are easy to partially implement.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:142:- Fixture fidelity: tool-call arguments and full tool results must remain as recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:154:| Tool-result prompt | `packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/tool-result-v1.ts` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:156:| Story tests | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` (planned) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:173:| TC-2.1a | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Aged large tool result renders through deterministic truncation with no provider call and stable output. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:174:| TC-2.2a | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Smooth-band summary is produced by queued inference work, not hot path. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:175:| TC-2.3a | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Result below 1000 tokens uses small-result target. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:176:| TC-2.3b | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Result from 1000 to 5000 tokens uses mid-result target. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-