{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts && rg -n \\\"full band|smooth band|tool result\\\" docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"// Epic 03 shared vocabulary: the thread-view types (tech design §Interface\n// Definitions). Shared so cli/sdk/tests import one home; the thread-view\n// domain owns the behavior, this module owns only the shapes.\n\nexport type Band = \"brief\" | \"detailed\" | \"smooth\";\n\nexport interface ViewProfile {\n  name: string;\n  // Target assembled size; whole-entry fills may land under or over (epic\n  // Data Contracts — the bound is a target, not a cap).\n  lowerBound: number;\n  // Band shares of the lower bound; must sum to 100 (AC-2.3).\n  percentages: { full: number; smooth: number; detailed: number; brief: number };\n}\n\n// A user profile entry as configured: a full profile under a new name, or a\n// field-wise override of a built-in (merged by name, AC-2.2). A partial entry\n// whose name matches no built-in has nothing to merge over and is rejected at\n// construction (FC-0.2's unknown-override violation).\nexport interface ViewProfileOverride {\n  name: string;\n  lowerBound?: number;\n  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\"percentages\"]>;\n}\n\n// Compact-time explicit parameters (AC-2.2): field-wise overrides of the\n// base profile, down to single band percentages — the same depth the CLI's\n// per-band flags override at. A nested-partial deepening of the tech\n// design's `Partial<ViewProfile>` sketch, which could not express a\n// single-band override.\nexport interface ViewCompactParams {\n  lowerBound?: number;\n  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\"percentages\"]>;\n}\n\n// Visibility-boundary budgets (Epic 03 AC-4.x as patched by Epic 05 AC-5.4):\n// max > target, both positive. The floor budget is retired — its job is done\n// structurally by the turn-end trigger (the open turn is untouchable) and the\n// never-evicted newest closed turn (Epic 05 DD-11).\nexport interface VisibilityBudgets {\n  maxTokens: number;\n  targetTokens: number;\n}\n\n// ── SDK assembly config (validated at construction, throws on nonsense\n// per the Epic 02 rule) ───────────────────────────────────────────\nexport interface SdkViewConfig {\n  profiles?: ViewProfileOverride[]; // merged over built-ins by name\n  visibility?: Partial<VisibilityBudgets>; // defaults: 64000 / 32000\n  compactThreshold?: number; // status trigger; default 160000\n}\n\n// Every optional filled by createSdk's central defaults; profiles resolved\n// to complete, validated entries keyed by name.\nexport interface ResolvedViewConfig {\n  profiles: Readonly<Record<string, ViewProfile>>;\n  visibility: VisibilityBudgets;\n  compactThreshold: number;\n}\n\n// ── pull / status shapes (the product crossing to the harness) ────\n//\n// The pull's array shape (Story 1, load-bearing for Stories 2–5): band\n// messages first — one `user` message per non-empty band, gradient order\n// brief → detailed → smooth, marker header + snapshot bytes verbatim — then\n// the tail in record order. Tail messages render by the message-kind mapping\n// table (tech design §Tail message rendering), the contract every later\n// story renders into:\n//\n//   | Message kind                       | Role      | Content shape |\n//   |------------------------------------|-----------|---------------|\n//   | user_prompt                        | user      | text verbatim |\n//   | assistant_text                     | assistant | text verbatim |\n//   | assistant_thinking                 | assistant | fenced: `[thinking]\\n<text>\\n[/thinking]` — included (the tail is full fidelity) |\n//   | tool_call                          | assistant | `[tool call · <name>] <compact args>` — deterministic arg rendering, abbreviation rule for oversized args |\n//   | tool_result (ahead of boundary)    | user      | `[tool result · <name>]\\n<full content>` |\n//   | tool_result (at-or-behind boundary)| user      | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (short-form ladder) |\n//   | runtime_note                       | user      | `[runtime note] <text>` |\nexport interface ViewMessage {\n  role: \"user\" | \"assistant\";\n  content: string;\n  band?: Band; // band absent ⇒ tail\n}\n\nexport interface ViewMeta {\n  compactPoint: number | null; // null ⇒ never compacted (AC-1.3)\n  coveredFrom: number | null;\n  boundaryPosition: number;\n  gapCount: number;\n  degradedCount: number;\n  viewId: string | null;\n  createdAt: string | null;\n}\n\nexport interface PullResult {\n  messages: ViewMessage[];\n  meta: ViewMeta;\n}\n\n// The stored active view row as `threadView.describe` exposes it (Epic 04\n// Story 3): the snapshot verbatim — arrangement, gaps, config, source-state\n// provenance, per-band stored token counts — never recomputed, never\n// repaired. Absent view ⇒ describe returns ok/null, mirroring status's\n// never-compacted behavior (DD-1).\nexport interface StoredView {\n  viewId: string;\n  createdAt: string;\n  compactPoint: number;\n  coveredFrom: number;\n  // null when explicit params overrode a named base at compact (the stored\n  // config carries the resolved truth either way).\n  profileName: string | null;\n  config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\n  // Every selected entry in served order, gap entries included (they are\n  // arrangement rows too; `gaps` carries their reasons).\n  arrangement: Array<{\n    band: Band;\n    subjectKind: \"chunk\" | \"turn\";\n    subjectId: string;\n    derivationUsed: string;\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/test-plan.md:107:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:25:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:33:  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:36:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:39:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:117:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:150:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:201:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:58:  - **TC-2.4** (AC-2.5): A tool result with content far past any rendering threshold (hundreds of KB) → read-back returns it byte-identical — via SDK, and repeated through the spawned CLI (stdin → read-back) in the process suite.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:108:| TC-2.4 | `test/projection.test.ts` + process suite | 300KB tool result → byte-identical read-back, SDK and spawned CLI |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:123:- Token estimates: tool calls count serialized `arguments`; tool results count the full `content` string; same insert as the message row; the util is called directly (no seam — golden counts beat stubs).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:270:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:351:        reason: \"Red-phase process suite: TC-2.4 spawned-CLI leg — 300KB tool result through real stdin reads back byte-identical via messages list\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:386:        - \"test/projection.test.ts: TC-2.4 300KB+ unicode tool result reads back byte-identical via SDK (full string equality on event payload and block content)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:391:        - \"test/cli-process-projection.test.ts: TC-2.4 spawned-CLI leg — 300KB tool result piped through real stdin, byte-identical through messages list on the built binary\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:51:| TC-2.1a | 2.1 | large tool result past visibility boundary | deterministic truncation, no provider call, identical input → identical output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:52:| TC-2.2a | 2.2 | tool result in smooth-band turn | summary produced by queued inference item, not hot path |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:57:| TC-2.4b | 2.4 | failed tool result | summary states failure outcome |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:60:| TC-2.6a | 2.6 | result truncated (full band) + summarized (smooth) | original full result intact in record |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:125:| Source-truth preserved | TC-2.6a | full tool result intact under truncation + summary |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:38:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:109:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:111:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:162:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:169:- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): Mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max → boundary unmoved, pulls byte-identical; the batch closing the turn commits → one advance, whole turns flipped oldest-first, no partial turn; a small next turn closes under max → no movement.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:252:3. Input bounding: whether `summarizeToolResult` truncates oversized inputs before the call (a 200k-char tool result on a small-context model), and where that bound lives. Dial-in will tune the value; design names the seam.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/00-prd.md:114:**Scenario 3: Old tool results age out of full visibility.** As the recent tail grows, older tool results become eligible for abbreviation, then activate in batches on budget pressure, so the prompt prefix changes in planned steps rather than every turn.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/00-prd.md:117:- AC-3.6: An activated tool result renders its summarized abbreviation, or deterministic truncation when the summary is not usable\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:254:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:325:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:327:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:151:- **TC-2.4** (AC-2.5): A tool result with content far past any rendering threshold (hundreds of KB) → read-back returns it byte-identical.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:154:- **TC-2.7** (AC-2.8): A batch with a prompt and a tool result → one `messages`-owned work item for prompt smoothing and one for tool-result summary, readable from the queue with `queued` status and correct source references.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:23:| `turn_rendering` | turn | composition | smooth band |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:35:> A tool result never falls below its truncation floor. The result always lands usable; the consuming operation never blocks and never omits a span. Every fallback **event** is **logged**. Only damage to the canonical **source** blocks; a missing or failed derivation degrades and continues.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:55:After this epic, every derivation has a deterministic floor and a uniform recovery cascade, so a not-ready or failed derivation degrades to an honest cruder rendering instead of blocking the operation or leaving a hole. Smart compact and turn construction always produce a usable result; only canonical source corruption stops them. Every fallback is recorded through a new logging surface so operators can see, query, and act on derivation health without runtime noise. Prompt smoothing gains a deterministic cleaning floor and a length gate; tool results split cleanly into deterministic full-band truncation and inference smooth-band summaries with per-tool guidance; the dead `tool_call_summary` type is removed; and runtime model/effort changes are recorded as typed blocks instead of opaque notes. The codebase is renamed from `form` to `derivation` throughout.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:79:- Tool-result rendering split: deterministic truncation for the full band (hot-path), inference summary for the smooth band (cold-path), with tiered targets and per-tool guidance scaffolding.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:188:A tool result is preserved in full in the record and rendered in shorter renderings for the views. The full-fidelity band shortens aged tool results by **deterministic truncation** (hot-path safe, no model). The smooth band uses an **inference summary** (`tool_result_summary`, cold-path). The summary targets a size tiered by the result's token count. Per-tool guidance shapes the summary because tool outputs differ in shape and in which parts matter. Tool *calls* (arguments) render as-is; they are not summarized.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:195:  - Given: a large tool result aged past the visibility boundary\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:196:  - When: the full band renders it\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:202:  - Given: a tool result in a turn assigned to the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:209:  - Given: a tool result under ~1000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:213:  - Given: a tool result between ~1000 and ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:217:  - Given: a tool result beyond ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:218:  - When: it is rendered for the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:224:  - Given: tool results from two different tools\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:228:  - Given: a failed tool result\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:243:**AC-2.6:** The full tool result is always retained in the record regardless of how it is rendered in any band.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:246:  - Given: a tool result that is truncated in the full band and summarized in the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:248:  - Then: the original full tool result is intact\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:250:**AC-2.7:** A tool result beyond the large-tier threshold satisfies its `tool_result_summary` by deterministic truncation and lands `ready` without inference (no inference work item is created for it).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:253:  - Given: a tool result beyond ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:336:**AC-3.8:** When turn-construction recovery resolves a not-ready component — by re-derivation, deterministic floor, or original-source floor — the resolved content is written back to the component's derivation record as `ready`, **except when a work item is still claimed or pending for that derivation**, in which case the record is left untouched (the floor is used in the rendering, but the in-flight worker is allowed to produce the real result). Persisted recovery outcomes land plain `ready`; there is no \"degraded\" state and no floor-used marker (no upgrade process consumes such a marker). The fallback *event* is logged; the canonical subject and any `ready` output carry no marker. A tool result's floor is deterministic truncation, never the raw full result.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:623:**Governing idea:** tool results render at the right fidelity per band, deterministically where it must be hot-path, by inference where it can be cold-path; calls render as-is.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:636:**Boundary / risk notes:** depends on the turn-summarization-at-close parity question (TD Q1); tool results never fall below truncation; pending and failed handled identically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:145:A closed turn queues exactly one `turn_derivation` item. A qualifying message queues exactly one item per applicable kind (`prompt_smoothing` for prompts, `tool_result_summary` for tool results). If Epic 02's turn derivation wants internal fan-out (smoothing, projection as separate steps), it fans out on its own side of the seam; the contract stays one-item-per-source-per-kind. This keeps the seam minimal, makes work-item ids derivable from their source, and matches the v1 reference's one-trigger-per-turn model, which worked.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:288:Two projection details are contractual rather than implementation-free. Block structure by kind: text-bearing kinds (`user_prompt`, `assistant_text`, `assistant_thinking`, `runtime_note`) project one text block; `tool_call` projects one block carrying `toolCallId`, `toolName`, and `arguments`; `tool_result` projects one block carrying `toolCallId`, the full `content`, and `isError`. Nothing splits, summarizes, or normalizes content at intake — AC-2.5's full preservation is the absence of any code path that could shorten it, which is why TC-2.4's hundreds-of-KB round-trip is a meaningful regression tripwire rather than a formality. Token estimates count each message's text content (for tool calls, the serialized arguments; for tool results, the full content string) through the one `token-counting` util, and the estimate lands on the message row in the same insert.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:18:3. **Split tool-result rendering** explicitly into deterministic-truncation (full band) vs inference-summary (smooth band) with tiered targets, and **remove `tool_call_summary`** (a derivation type that exists but is being dropped).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md:303:- **Source-truth vs derived:** full tool result preserved while truncated/summarized (AC-2.6); recovery never mutates canonical source.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/tech-design.md:85:| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/epic.md:92:- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/epic.md:110:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:13:**Objective:** render tool results at the right fidelity per band while retaining full source results and removing `tool_call_summary`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:34:  - Given: a large tool result aged past the visibility boundary\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:35:  - When: the full band renders it\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:41:  - Given: a tool result in a turn assigned to the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:48:  - Given: a tool result under ~1000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:52:  - Given: a tool result between ~1000 and ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:56:  - Given: a tool result beyond ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:57:  - When: it is rendered for the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:63:  - Given: tool results from two different tools\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:67:  - Given: a failed tool result\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:82:**AC-2.6:** The full tool result is always retained in the record regardless of how it is rendered in any band.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:85:  - Given: a tool result that is truncated in the full band and summarized in the smooth band\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:87:  - Then: the original full tool result is intact\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:89:**AC-2.7:** A tool result beyond the large-tier threshold satisfies its `tool_result_summary` by deterministic truncation and lands `ready` without inference (no inference work item is created for it).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:92:  - Given: a tool result beyond ~5000 tokens\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:110:Tool calls are not summarized. Removing `tool_call_summary` must reach the derivation kind set, work-queue registry, compose part plans, provider interface, deterministic provider, and prompt surface. Full source tool results remain canonical and intact.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:121:- Fixture fidelity: tool-call arguments and full tool results must remain as recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:152:| TC-2.1a | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Aged large tool result renders through deterministic truncation with no provider call and stable output. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:157:| TC-2.4a | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Different tool results receive keyed prompt guidance and preserve outcome/status. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:158:| TC-2.4b | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Failed tool result summary states the failure outcome. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:161:| TC-2.6a | `packages/lhc/test/tool-result-rendering.test.ts` | Full source tool result remains intact after truncation and summary renderings. |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:181:- Do not delete the full tool result to make truncation tests pass.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:183:- Do not create inference work for large-tier tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:187:- Entrypoint: recorded tool result reaches message/turn derivation through existing work-queue drain and turn composition.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:205:- Full source tool results remain intact.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/02-tool-result-rendering.md:206:- Large smooth-band tool results land `ready` via truncation without inference work.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:50:- **Two zones, two mechanisms:** the **full band** uses deterministic **truncation** (can run in the hot path); the **smooth band** uses inference **summary** (cannot run in the hot path). Truncation is already in use; summary is the added inference.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:55:  - The token thresholds and percentages are a first pass. Subsequent passes dial in `tool_result_summary` based on more aspects of the tool result — **including which tool it is** — and will be added later.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:93:**Smooth turn = same membership as the full-fidelity turn.** The only difference: in the full band some tool results are **truncated**; in the smooth band they are **summarized**.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:106:- **Tool result** — if the summary is ready, use it. If not, attempt to regenerate; failing that, fall to **deterministic truncation**. **NEVER copy the full tool result.** There is never a reason you can't truncate a string before writing the result-summary field — so the floor for a tool result is always at least truncation, never the raw full result.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:111:**Same principle across components.** Lee: \"we're keeping the same principle that we're doing with the user prompt.\" Try for the real thing; else deterministic floor; else original (except tool result never goes below truncation); continue; don't block; no degraded state. On any fallback, log it (see logging section).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:130:**Chunk summaries take `lower_band_projection` as input, NOT `turn_rendering`.** The thing chunks summarize is the coarser per-turn projection, not the rich smooth-band turn (which keeps all thinking/tools). This is why turn derivation produces two derivations: `turn_rendering` (rich → smooth band) and `lower_band_projection` (stripped → chunk-summary input). Lee's recollection (\"constructed slightly differently\") is correct and already built this way.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:207:- At the wire boundary, **one band → one message.** The whole smooth band (and likewise detailed, brief) collapses into a single `user`-role message with a `[context · <band>]` header + concatenated content. The tail renders each message to its own wire message with its natural role.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:209:- **Caching is fine with this** (confirmed): the bottom three bands are a stable prefix between compacts; only the full band grows at the end; the only prefix churn is the visibility-boundary truncation, already optimized. Flattening doesn't hurt cache; if anything one big band message has fewer block boundaries to invalidate than many separate messages.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:211:### Candidate refinement: smooth band as user/assistant pairs (dial-in)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:212:- Lee is OK with detailed and brief bands as-is. The **smooth band** is the one worth possibly reshaping.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:214:- Upsides: (1) the model's own past work is voiced as **assistant** rather than narrated back to it as `user` (fixes an attribution smear); (2) partially fixes consecutive-`user`-message alternation (smooth band becomes alternating pairs, not one more `user` blob).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/notes/derivation-cascade-decisions.md:215:- Cost: smooth band is no longer \"one message\" — 2 messages per smooth turn. Cache-neutral (still a stable prefix between compacts).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:56:| Tool full-band rendering | Full-band aged tool results use deterministic truncation with no provider | Story 2 | TC-2.1a |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:58:| Tool large-result floor | Large tool results satisfy `tool_result_summary` by truncation without inference work | Story 2 | TC-2.7a |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:254:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:325:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:327:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:37:  - **TC-2.4** (AC-2.5): A tool result with content far past any rendering threshold (hundreds of KB) → read-back returns it byte-identical — via SDK, and repeated through the spawned CLI (stdin → read-back) in the process suite.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:48:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:87:| TC-2.4 | `test/projection.test.ts` + process suite | 300KB tool result → byte-identical read-back, SDK and spawned CLI |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:102:- Token estimates: tool calls count serialized `arguments`; tool results count the full `content` string; same insert as the message row; the util is called directly (no seam — golden counts beat stubs).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/03-turn-construction-recovery-cascade.md:18:- Deterministic floor then original-source fallback, except tool results never fall below truncation.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/03-turn-construction-recovery-cascade.md:94:**AC-3.8:** When turn-construction recovery resolves a not-ready component — by re-derivation, deterministic floor, or original-source floor — the resolved content is written back to the component's derivation record as `ready`, **except when a work item is still claimed or pending for that derivation**, in which case the record is left untouched (the floor is used in the rendering, but the in-flight worker is allowed to produce the real result). Persisted recovery outcomes land plain `ready`; there is no \"degraded\" state and no floor-used marker (no upgrade process consumes such a marker). The fallback *event* is logged; the canonical subject and any `ready` output carry no marker. A tool result's floor is deterministic truncation, never the raw full result.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md:23:- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:58:  - **TC-2.4** (AC-2.5): A tool result with content far past any rendering threshold (hundreds of KB) → read-back returns it byte-identical — via SDK, and repeated through the spawned CLI (stdin → read-back) in the process suite.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:108:| TC-2.4 | `test/projection.test.ts` + process suite | 300KB tool result → byte-identical read-back, SDK and spawned CLI |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:123:- Token estimates: tool calls count serialized `arguments`; tool results count the full `content` string; same insert as the message row; the util is called directly (no seam — golden counts beat stubs).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:270:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:441:        reason: \"Red-phase process suite: TC-2.4 spawned-CLI leg — 300KB tool result through real stdin reads back byte-identical via messages list\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:476:        - \"test/projection.test.ts: TC-2.4 300KB+ unicode tool result reads back byte-identical via SDK (full string equality on event payload and block content)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:481:        - \"test/cli-process-projection.test.ts: TC-2.4 spawned-CLI leg — 300KB tool result piped through real stdin, byte-identical through messages list on the built binary\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:620:        - \"AC-2.5 / TC-2.4 on current-schema threads: 300KB+ tool result content reads back byte-identical through SDK and the spawned CLI suite.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:25:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:53:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/05-derivation-work-queueing.md:34:  - **TC-2.7** (AC-2.8): Prompt + tool result batch → `w-m1-prompt_smoothing` and `w-m2-tool_result_summary`, owner `messages`, status `queued`, correct sourceRefs.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/05-derivation-work-queueing.md:89:| TC-2.7 | `test/work-queue.test.ts` 