ndering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:202:- Do not delete the full tool result to make truncation tests pass.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:204:- Do not create inference work for large-tier tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:208:- Entrypoint: recorded tool result reaches message/turn derivation through existing work-queue drain and turn composition.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:226:- Full source tool results remain intact.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:227:- Large smooth-band tool results land `ready` via truncation without inference work.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:286:| TC-2.1a | 2.1 | large tool result past visibility boundary | deterministic truncation, no provider call, identical input → identical output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:287:| TC-2.2a | 2.2 | tool result in smooth-band turn | summary produced by queued inference item, not hot path |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:292:| TC-2.4b | 2.4 | failed tool result | summary states failure outcome |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:295:| TC-2.6a | 2.6 | result truncated (full band) + summarized (smooth) | original full result intact in record |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/02-tool-result-rendering/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:360:| Source-truth preserved | TC-2.6a | full tool result intact under truncation + summary |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:26:- **DD-7: Input bounding is an adapter seam with a generous default.** Question 3, resolved: `summarizeToolResult` content over `inference.maxInputChars` (default 200 000) is truncated head-and-tail with a marker before prompt rendering. The bound exists so a pathological tool result cannot blow a small-context model; the value is a dial-in tunable, the seam is design.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:29:- **DD-10: Whole-turn eviction via `turn_id` grouping; turnless results degrade to singleton groups.** The zone walk groups tool results by `turn_id` (the message column), oldest group first by the group's lowest `source_event_order`. A `turn_id IS NULL` tool result (turnless intake is legal) is its own group — whole-turn semantics degenerate to whole-message for messages that belong to no turn, which preserves the epic's \"no turn is ever partially flipped\" without inventing membership.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:58:  - **TC-2.4** (AC-2.5): A tool result with content far past any rendering threshold (hundreds of KB) → read-back returns it byte-identical — via SDK, and repeated through the spawned CLI (stdin → read-back) in the process suite.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:108:| TC-2.4 | `test/projection.test.ts` + process suite | 300KB tool result → byte-identical read-back, SDK and spawned CLI |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:123:- Token estimates: tool calls count serialized `arguments`; tool results count the full `content` string; same insert as the message row; the util is called directly (no seam — golden counts beat stubs).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:270:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:443:        reason: \"Red-phase process suite: TC-2.4 spawned-CLI leg — 300KB tool result through real stdin reads back byte-identical via messages list\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:478:        - \"test/projection.test.ts: TC-2.4 300KB+ unicode tool result reads back byte-identical via SDK (full string equality on event payload and block content)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:483:        - \"test/cli-process-projection.test.ts: TC-2.4 spawned-CLI leg — 300KB tool result piped through real stdin, byte-identical through messages list on the built binary\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:622:        - \"AC-2.5 / TC-2.4 on current-schema threads: 300KB+ tool result content reads back byte-identical through SDK and the spawned CLI suite.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:254:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:325:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:327:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:217:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/st