oundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:269:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:340:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:342:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:536:        - \"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:46:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-010.md:46:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-010.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/03-view-contents-report/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:44:- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/03-view-contents-report/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:288:        - \"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 remains verified: tail cost is measured from served pull tail, including short-form tool results behind the visibility boundary.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/03-view-contents-report/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:419:        - \"TC-2.2's boundary-advanced fixture relies on Epic 03's floor-protection behavior (the newest 80-token result stays full) to keep one abridged and one full tool result coexisting in the tail; if visibility advance semantics ever change, the fixture's expected counts move with them\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/03-view-contents-report/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:533:        - \"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2: inspect.view measures tail messages from threadView.pull; the boundary-advanced fixture asserts one abridged and one full tool result and verifies tail.tokens/loadCost.tailTokens equal measured served tail.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:265:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:336:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:338:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:302:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-012.md:46:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc