ndary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:57:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:60:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:138:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:171:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:222:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:272:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:343:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:345:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:656:        - \"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:726:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:740:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-013.md:46:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-013.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:66:- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:302:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:265:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:336:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:338:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:302:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `