m.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:669:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:265:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:336:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:338:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:46:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:66:- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:302:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:302:Representative boundary proofs, not full TC repetition: `new-thread` → `resolve` round-trip; `message-events` via real stdin (including the 300KB tool result); TTY/empty stdin → `empty_stdin`, exit 1; one validation failure → JSON error shape, exit 1; `--help` and unknown command exit codes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:46:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:46:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:54:  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:57:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:60:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:138:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:168:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:219:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:269:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:340:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:342:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:475:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:489:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:655:        - \"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:46:- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:265:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:336:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:338:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:66:- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:12:**Objective:** the tail self-regulates. Old tool results age to short form in batches when a budget breaks — log rotation, not per-turn churn.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:29:- **AC-4.1**: Each thread carries one visibility boundary. Tail tool results at-or-behind it render the short form; ahead of it, full. Non-tool-result content is never affected by the boundary.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:33:  - **TC-4.1** (AC-4.3): Intake tool results totaling under max → boundary unmoved; pulls byte-identical across batches. Cross max with one more batch → boundary advances once to target; exactly one batch of results flipped, oldest-first; next under-max batch → no movement.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:36:  - **TC-4.3** (AC-4.5): Single monster turn: tool results exceeding max within one open turn → boundary advances into the turn but stops at the protected set; the newest whole results (combined tokens ≥ floor) render full; oversized-newest leg: a single result larger than the floor is protected alone; the turn's own text messages all render full.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/test-plan.md:73:**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whole-message rule): protected set = newest tool results joined until the set's sum first reaches/exceeds floor; an oversized newest result is protected alone and the zone legally sits above target (or max) that batch; boundary never lands inside the protected set; at least the newest result is full whenever any exists.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:46:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:54:  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:57:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:60:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:138:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:171:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:222:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:272:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:343:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:345:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:630:        - \"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:700:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-008.md:714:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:66:- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:13:Two cost structures dominate the design, and they pull in the same direction: do nothing per-turn. The pull sits on the hot path between the user's action and the model call, so it must be reads and string assembly — every judgment (which chunk in which band, which tool result short) was made earlier by an explicit operation. And the harness caches its prompt prefix; every byte that changes above the newest content is money. The MVP's tool-result truncation re-decided every result's visibility on every message — the prefix churned every turn, which at Opus-class pricing is roughly $0.15 per turn, forever. The replacement design changes the prompt only at discrete, attributable events: a compact (explicit, rare), or a boundary advance (batched, budget-triggered). Between those events, identical pulls return identical bytes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:15:The view is a snapshot, not a projection-on-read. A compact selects the band arrangement, renders each band's text from stored artifacts, and stores the rendered snapshot; pulls serve those bytes verbatim until the next compact. Record mutations and repairs land in the record immediately and become visible at the next compact — this was settled deliberately in the epic round (edit-then-recompact, no live view patching, no force-refresh) because curation is an occasional batch act, not a runtime channel. The one self-acting piece is the boundary: old tool results in the tail age to short form in batches when a budget breaks, because tool bloat accumulates without anyone deciding it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:161:  position INTEGER NOT NULL,           -- source event order (compact_point's coordinate system); tool results at-or-behind render short\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:166:One active view: `thread_view` holds at most one row; compact's transaction deletes and inserts (AC-2.6 — the cascade clears bands with it). The full band is not stored — it *is* the record after `compact_point`, read live at pull. `view_boundary` is a singleton row seeded at migration to position 0 (everything full). Budgets live in config, not rows.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:180:3. **Detailed band:** chunks entirely older than the smooth band's coverage, newest-first, same fill rule against `L × detailed%`, using `chunk_summary_detailed` counts.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:182:5. Turns closed but not yet chunked that fall between detailed/brief coverage and the smooth band stay in the **smooth band's coverage walk** (they are turns; they take the smooth representation and its budget) — bands are defined by *representation*, not by strict time strata.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:189:After intake commit (flush of `ctx.onCommit`): `SUM(token_estimate)` over tool-result messages with `source_event_order > boundary.position` and `source_event_order > compact_point` (one indexed query). The boundary is a **source event order** position everywhere — storage, interfaces, and prose; it shares the compact point's coordinate system. If sum ≤ `max`: return. Else walk those results oldest-first, accumulating flips, until remaining sum ≤ `target` **or** the next flip would touch the protected set. The floor protects **whole messages**: walking newest-backward, tool results join the protected set until its sum first reaches or exceeds `floor` — so at least the newest tool result is always protected when any exists, an oversized newest result is protected alone even though it exceeds the floor by itself, and the full zone may consequently sit above `target` (or even `max`) until newer batches or a compact create room (AC-4.5). Write the new position (own short transaction), done. Never backward; compact reset writes `position = compact_point` inside the compact transaction. Failures: caught, logged to stderr-level diagnostics, never thrown into intake's caller — the condition stays visible because status computes the same sum live (AC-4.9's \"visible in status\" is structural, not stored).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:198:| Tail tool result (short) | `tool_result_summary` | deterministic truncation (existing Epic 01 abbreviation rule) | — | n/a (raw content always exists) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:212:| `tool_result` (ahead of boundary) | `user` | `[tool result · <name>]\\n<full content>` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:213:| `tool_result` (at-or-behind boundary) | `user` | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (per the short-form ladder) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:219:user:      [tool result · read_file · abridged]\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:227:user:      [tool result · edit]\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:235:**Covers:** AC-1.1–1.7. The hot-path read. Resolve thread → read view header + band rows (if any) → read tail messages after `compact_point` (deleted-filtered, record order) → read boundary → format: band messages (one `user` message per non-empty band, marker header + snapshot bytes verbatim), then tail messages (tool results at-or-behind boundary in short form), return with `ViewMeta`. No view row: whole record is tail from event 1 (AC-1.3).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:25:**Mental model:** \"the record is the truth; the view is what the model sees. A compact rebuilds the view from materials that already exist. Between compacts the view is stable: my edits and repairs land in the record now and show up in the view at the next compact. Nothing changes my prompt behind my back except old tool results aging out in batches.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:36:4. **Tool-result visibility** — one boundary marker per thread; tool results behind it render short, ahead of it render full; advances in batches under budget pressure only; never moves backward.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:46:| 4 | Tool-Result Visibility | Batched aging of old tool results; budget-triggered, floor-protected, never backward |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:86:The harness asks for the current context. The pull reads the active view's stored band snapshot (if a compact has run), reads the tail — messages after the compact point — applies the visibility boundary to tail tool results, and returns the assembled message array. Reads and deterministic formatting only. The pull writes nothing and decides nothing; every judgment call (band membership, visibility, gap handling) was made earlier by a compact, a boundary advance, or Epic 02's derivations.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:98:- **AC-1.5**: Tail tool results render by boundary position: at-or-behind the boundary renders the short form, ahead of it renders full content. All non-tool-result content in the tail renders full, always.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:107:- **TC-1.4** (AC-1.5): With the boundary mid-tail, pull → tool results behind it are short-form, ahead of it full, prompts and assistant text full everywhere.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:166:Old tool results are the tail's bloat: one agentic turn can dump a hundred thousand tokens of file reads and build output. The MVP re-decided every result's visibility on every message, churning the prompt cache every turn. This design replaces that with one marker per thread and a log-rotation policy: nothing happens until the full-visibility zone outgrows its budget, then one batched advance, then quiet again.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:168:The rule set, complete: tool results at-or-behind the boundary render short (Epic 02's summary when usable, deterministic truncation otherwise); tool results ahead of it render full; nothing else is ever affected — prompts, assistant text, and thinking always render full. After an intake batch commits, the advance check runs as a thread-view maintenance step, triggered through the SDK's post-commit seam (Epic 02's onCommit pattern) — automatic, never a host-remembered call, and outside the intake transaction, so intake's outcome never depends on it. One indexed sum measures the full-zone tool tokens; if it exceeds the max budget, the boundary advances oldest-first until the zone is at-or-under the target budget; otherwise nothing happens. A failed advance leaves the boundary unchanged and the over-budget condition visible in the status read; the next batch's check re-evaluates the same condition, so the debt is bounded by one batch. The boundary never advances into the protected floor — the most recent stretch of tool output stays full even mid-monster-turn — and never moves backward: a flipped result stays flipped. A compact resets the boundary to the compact point, because the old tail just became bands.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:174:- **AC-4.1**: Each thread carries one visibility boundary. Tail tool results at-or-behind it render the short form; ahead of it, full. Non-tool-result content is never affected by the boundary.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:186:- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.3): Intake tool results totaling under max → boundary unmoved; pulls byte-identical across batches. Cross max with one more batch → boundary advances once to target; exactly one batch of results flipped, oldest-first; next under-max batch → no movement.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:188:- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.5): Single monster turn: tool results exceeding max within one open turn → boundary advances into the turn but stops at the protected set; the newest whole results (combined tokens ≥ floor) render full; oversized-newest leg: a single result larger than the floor is protected alone; the turn's own text messages all render full.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:31:- **AC-1.5** *(default-boundary leg; boundary-active leg lands in Story 4)*: Tail tool results render by boundary position: at-or-behind the boundary renders the short form, ahead of it renders full content. All non-tool-result content in the tail renders full, always.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:32:  - **TC-1.4** (AC-1.5) *(owned here; boundary seeded below-SDK via the sanctioned `test/fixtures/` helper — boundary mechanics owned by Story 4's TC-4.x)*: With the boundary mid-tail, pull → tool results behind it are short-form, ahead of it full, prompts and assistant text full everywhere.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:66:| Short-form ladder (tail tool result row) | tech-design.md L198 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:66:- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:46:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:54:  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:57:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:60:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:138:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:171:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:222:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:272:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:343:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:345:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:630:        - \"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:700:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-009.md:714:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:66:- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:46:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:54:  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:57:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:60:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:138:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:171:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:222:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:272:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:343:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:345:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:586:        - \"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:656:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:670:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:212:**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whole-message rule): protected set = newest tool results joined until the set's sum first reaches/exceeds floor; an oversized newest result is protected alone and the zone legally sits above target (or max) that batch; boundary never lands inside the protected set; at least the newest result is full whenever any exists.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:46:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:54:  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:57:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:60:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:138:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:168:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:219:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:269:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:340:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:342:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:46:- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:54:  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:57:  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:60:  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:138:| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:171:| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:222:- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:272:**Boundary fixtures** — `test/fixtures/` gains `seedTurnedToolResults(db, turns: { results: number[] }[])`: closed turns with tool results of given token estimates, plus turnless-result and open-turn variants. Built on the existing Epic 03 fixture helpers; token estimates seeded via content sized to the estimator (existing pattern from view-boundary tests).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:343:- the `turn_end` batch commits → one advance; flipped set = whole oldest turns (every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together; assert per-turn all-or-nothing)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:345:- turnless tool result (singleton group, DD-10) evicts whole-message\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:656:        - \"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:726:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:740:        evidence: \"AC-5.3 requires that the newest closed turn is never evicted, and the story technical notes state `newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction` while `turn_id IS NULL` rows are singleton groups. In `boundary.ts`, `advanceDecision` builds `candidates` by only filtering the open turn, then excludes `candidates.length - 1` as the newest candidate group. When a turnless singleton appears after the newest closed turn, that singleton becomes the excluded newest candidate, leaving the newest closed turn eligible for eviction. A production-path probe through `createSdk` and real `intakeStream.messageEvents` with budgets 100/60 and groups t1=30 closed, t2=70 closed, trailing turnless=60 failed with `newest closed turn was evicted: expected boundary 3, observed 7`; observed boundary 7 is t2's tool result, so the newest closed turn flipped. Existing tests cover a turnless singleton before the final closed turn and a newest-closed case without a trailing turnless singleton, leaving this legal shape uncovered.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:212:**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whole-message rule): protected set = newest tool results joined until the set's sum first reaches/exceeds floor; an oversized newest result is protected alone and the zone legally sits above target (or max) that batch; boundary never lands inside the protected set; at least the newest result is full whenever any exists.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:212:**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whole-message rule): protected set = newest tool results joined until the set's sum first reaches/exceeds floor; an oversized newest result is protected alone and the zone legally sits above target (or max) that batch; boundary never lands inside the protected set; at least the newest result is full whenever any exists.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:33:**Objective:** the tail self-regulates. Old tool results age to short form in batches when a budget breaks — log rotation, not per-turn churn.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:50:- **AC-4.1**: Each thread carries one visibility boundary. Tail tool results at-or-behind it render the short form; ahead of it, full. Non-tool-result content is never affected by the boundary.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:54:  - **TC-4.1** (AC-4.3): Intake tool results totaling under max → boundary unmoved; pulls byte-identical across batches. Cross max with one more batch → boundary advances once to target; exactly one batch of results flipped, oldest-first; next under-max batch → no movement.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:57:  - **TC-4.3** (AC-4.5): Single monster turn: tool results exceeding max within one open turn → boundary advances into the turn but stops at the protected set; the newest whole results (combined tokens ≥ floor) render full; oversized-newest leg: a single result larger than the floor is protected alone; the turn's own text messages all render full.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:219:**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whole-message rule): protected set = newest tool results joined until the set's sum first reaches/exceeds floor; an oversized newest result is protected alone and the zone legally sits above target (or max) that batch; boundary never lands inside the protected set; at least the newest result is full whenever any exists.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:212:**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whole-message rule): protected set = newest tool results joined until the set's sum first reaches/exceeds floor; an oversized newest result is protected alone and the zone legally sits above target (or max) that batch; boundary never lands inside the protected set; at least the newest result is full whenever any exists.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/05-render-targets/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:221:**Boundary G1 — trajectory:** scripted intake sequence (sums crossing max twice, one monster turn) → committed expected positions after each batch. Floor legs (whol